{
  "name": "Cold Reply Setter Automation",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Cold Reply Setter Automation\n\nThis workflow expects your cold email platform to POST reply data into the webhook.\n\nRequired webhook body fields:\n- `lead_id`\n- `thread_id`\n- `prospect_email`\n- `prospect_name` (optional)\n- `reply_text`\n- `send_reply_url` -> endpoint that actually sends the reply in your cold email tool\n- `google_doc_url` -> Google Doc with setter playbook / reply instructions\n- `sheet_document_id` -> Google Sheet ID\n- `sheet_name` -> tab name\n\nOptional webhook body fields:\n- `send_bearer_token`\n- `original_subject`\n- `campaign_name`\n- `company_name`\n- `sender_name`\n- `sender_email`\n\nGoogle Sheet expected columns:\n- `lead_id`\n- `thread_id`\n- `prospect_email`\n- `classification`\n- `sheet_status`\n- `reply_subject`\n- `reply_body`\n- `last_reply_text`\n- `updated_at`\n\nAfter import:\n1. Connect your Google Docs credential.\n2. Connect your Google Sheets credential.\n3. Connect your OpenAI credential.\n4. Point `send_reply_url` to your cold email platform reply endpoint.\n5. Make sure your sheet already has the columns above.\n\nIf your send API needs a different body shape, only edit the `Send Reply` node.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      },
